        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "24c4196ace97efdb28b0df9e759470e4bada3e7e",
            "parents": [
                "410ccd62a1841eaa90e7364c4c1e58cd7cdaada8"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/26/92126/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Daniel Hufnagle",
                "email": "danielchufnagle@gmail.com",
                "username": "danielhufnagle"
            },
            "createdOn": 1783526021,
            "author": {
                "name": "Daniel Hufnagle",
                "email": "danielchufnagle@gmail.com",
                "username": "danielhufnagle"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I think we need to sell this a bit more. I know at IBM we're pushing people towards UBI because of the security aspects (same rigorous testing and security patching as RHEL). So lets drop the \"Ideally\" and replace \"would\" with \"will\".\n\nAlso we recently ran into some very painful issues with Ubuntu and how it uses http for a lot of it's default updates (more and more environments are dropping http support for security reasons).\n\nMy main concern is that OpenBMC tends to be fairly cutting edge so we may run into situations where UBI does not have the latest package required by OpenBMC but as this script is also used for our older releases, it will be nice to have a more stable and supported container distro like UBI."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Daniel Hufnagle",
                        "email": "danielchufnagle@gmail.com",
                        "username": "danielhufnagle"
                    },
                    "message": "Modified the language in the commit message accordingly"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yocto doesn't really claim that RHEL will work but they do claim Fedora will work.  We don't actually use Fedora anyhow so I'm not really caring too much about this branch in the script, but it seems like we get better support with Fedora.  You need to reconcile IBM/RH's philosophy with the OSS world to justify this move...\n\nhttps://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-yocto/tree/meta-poky/conf/distro/poky.conf?id=366fa2f21bfb0d9c4de492e0204a0dd38ce241ab"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Daniel Hufnagle",
                        "email": "danielchufnagle@gmail.com",
                        "username": "danielhufnagle"
                    },
                    "message": "Makes sense. Thank you."
                }
            ],
